  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be retained in accordance with the following approved plans:\rH-0360 REV V1 - Elevations\rH-0360 REV V1 - Floor Plans\rLocation Plan\rExisting Block Plan\rDesign, Access and Planning Statement\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 7 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within 3 months of the date of this decision notice, rooflights shall be installed above the Bedroom 2 and combined kitchen/dining area, and a window shall be installed to the rear elevation of the kitchen in the loft area as required by the standards of the Council. Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter. \rReason: In the interests of amenity for present and future occupiers.\r",
    "Within three months of this permission, details of the siting, number and design of 8 long stay cycle parking shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details before it is occupied.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards.\r",
    "Within three months of this permission, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste shall be provided within the development in pursuance of the HMO hereby approved and in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Waste and Recycling Planning Storage Guidance ENV 08/162. This shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority prior to occupation. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r"
  ],
